[14.357152, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[378.107713, "o", "KLEE is installed and verified.\r\n\r\n## Installed\r\n\r\n- **KLEE 3.3** (Release, assertions on) — `/usr/local/bin/klee`\r\n- **LLVM 16.0.6** (`clang-16`) as the toolchain\r\n- **STP 2.4.1** as the solver backend, built with MiniSat, installed under `/usr/local`\r\n- **No uClibc** — `KLEE_UCLIBC_PATH` left unset and uClibc runtime not built\r\n- Header at `/usr/local/include/klee/klee.h`, runtime bitcode under `/usr/local/lib/klee/runtime`\r\n- Sources retained in `/opt/src/{klee,stp,minisat}`\r\n\r\n## Environment (`~/.bashrc`)\r\n\r\nExports are placed **before** Ubuntu's non-interactive `return` guard so `source ~/.bashrc` works in test shells:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nexport PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:$PATH\"\r\nexport CPATH=\"/usr/local/include${CPATH:+:$CPATH}\"\r\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"/usr/local/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\nIn a clean non-interactive shell with `~/.bashrc` sourced:\r\n\r\n- `command -v klee` → `/usr/local/bin/klee`\r\n- `$CPATH` → `/usr/local/include`\r\n- `#include <klee/klee.h>` compiles with `clang-16` **without** `-I`\r\n- A symbolic-execution run reports `KLEE: Using STP solver backend`, `SAT solver: MiniSat`, finds the seeded assertion, and generates test cases\r\n\r\nOne note: KLEE's POSIX runtime is disabled. Its upstream `runtime/POSIX/fd.c` uses legacy x86 `__NR_*` syscall constants that glibc does not define on aarch64, so it cannot compile here; this also aligns with the no-uClibc requirement. Core KLEE symbolic execution works fully.\r\n"]
